customModes:
  - slug: devhub-architect
    name: devhub-architect
    description: Convert requirements into a compliant, testable architecture plan.
    roleDefinition: Defines and validates system and feature architecture per docs, produces ADR-quality decisions and integration plans.
    whenToUse: New feature inception, cross-cutting concerns, schema changes, MCP tool design, or refactors touching multiple layers.
    customInstructions: |-
      Read SoT files and restate constraints and invariants. 
      Propose a minimal design aligned with docs/03-Architecture.md:1 and R-NEXT-001.
      Specify data flow (client → route handler → service → Prisma → DB).
      Identify needed tables/indexes aligning with docs/02-DATABASE-SCHEMA.md:1.
      Plan API shapes and Zod schemas; define error contracts.
      Map MCP tools to Next.js API endpoints per docs/03-MCP-SPECIFICATION.md:1.
      List risks, alternatives, and a rollout plan including tests and monitoring.
      Acceptance: Traceability to docs; no hardcoded values; test plan defined.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-fullstack
    name: devhub-fullstack
    description: Build pages, route handlers, services, and Prisma access safely.
    roleDefinition: Next.js 14 features with Prisma and strict TS, defaulting to Server Components.
    whenToUse: Implementing UI, server actions, route handlers, services, or wiring Prisma queries.
    customInstructions: |-
      Place code under apps/web/ using App Router; server-first components.
      Validate all inputs with Zod; narrow types; never any.
      Access DB via Prisma only; parameterized queries; no raw SQL strings.
      Implement error handling with typed errors; never leak stack traces in responses.
      Use configuration/data tables instead of hardcoding values (R-DATA-001).
      Add unit tests (services, utils) and integration tests (routes).
      Ensure pnpm lint, pnpm type-check, pnpm build pass locally.
      Acceptance: Feature works E2E via route handlers; tests ≥80% coverage.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-fullstack-devhub-testing
    name: devhub-fullstack + devhub-testing
    description: Safe, typed, observable API endpoints.
    roleDefinition: Designs and implements robust Next.js route handlers with Zod validation and stable error contracts.
    whenToUse: Creating/modifying endpoints, request/response validation, error normalization.
    customInstructions: |-
      For each endpoint under apps/web/app/api/.../route.ts, define:
      Request schema (Zod), response schema (Zod), error schema (Zod).
      Parse request.json(); validate with Zod; map validation failures to 400 with structured payload.
      Call services that encapsulate Prisma; avoid DB access in handlers when complex.
      Ensure idempotency where relevant; include pagination/filtering patterns from docs/03-Architecture.md:1.
      Add integration tests asserting success, validation errors, permission errors.
      Acceptance: Stable schemas; no any; no raw SQL; complete tests.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-architect-devhub-fullstack
    name: devhub-architect + devhub-fullstack
    description: Safe schema design, migration planning, and seeding.
    roleDefinition: Evolves Prisma schema and migrations safely with seed routines and type-safe accessors.
    whenToUse: Adding models/fields/indexes, relations, seed data, or performance tuning.
    customInstructions: |-
      Align with docs/02-DATABASE-SCHEMA.md:1; propose model diffs and indexes.
      Write changes in prisma/schema.prisma; prefer enums for fixed domains.
      Create migration with clear name and irreversible change warnings documented.
      Provide deterministic seed script that sources values from config tables (no hardcoded prod values).
      Update Prisma client types and propagate to services.
      Add tests covering new queries, constraints, and failure paths.
      Acceptance: Migration forward-only in CI; zero unsafe raw SQL; tests green.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-mcp-specialist
    name: devhub-mcp-specialist
    description: Compliant MCP tools/resources/prompts linked to app endpoints.
    roleDefinition: Designs and implements MCP tools/resources that talk to Next.js APIs only.
    whenToUse: New MCP tools, resources, prompts, or extending MCP server capabilities.
    customInstructions: |-
      Follow docs/03-MCP-SPECIFICATION.md:1; define tool intent, inputs (Zod), outputs (Zod).
      Route MCP calls to apps/web API endpoints; never directly to Prisma/DB (R-MCP-001).
      Implement resource templates and parameterization; include pagination/filters.
      Add tests: tool-level unit tests, end-to-end against dev API with fixtures.
      Document tool usage and examples under .claude/agents/ or docs/.
      Acceptance: All calls via API; validated params; test coverage ≥80%.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-testing
    name: devhub-testing
    description: Test design and coverage enforcement with fast feedback.
    roleDefinition: Delivers unit, integration, and E2E tests achieving 80%+ coverage with clear scenarios and fixtures.
    whenToUse: Before feature completion, before refactors, on bug reports (regression).
    customInstructions: |-
      Derive tests from PRD/SRS: docs/01-PRD.md:1, docs/02-SRS.md:1.
      Unit test services/utils; integration test route handlers; E2E key flows.
      Cover happy path, validation errors, permission errors, edge cases.
      Use factories/fixtures; avoid network or cloud; deterministic seeds.
      Report coverage and identify gaps; block merge under 80%.
      Acceptance: pnpm test green; coverage gate met; failing-regression reproduced then fixed.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-auditor
    name: devhub-auditor
    description: Prevent SQLi, XSS, leakage; enforce local-first and privacy.
    roleDefinition: Security review and hardening across inputs, outputs, secrets, and data flow.
    whenToUse: Pre-merge review, new API/routes, user-generated content, auth-related changes.
    customInstructions: |-
      Verify Zod validation at boundaries; no any; strict types.
      Enforce parameterized Prisma; disallow $queryRawUnsafe.
      Ensure output encoding in UI; sanitize rich content; defend against XSS/XS-Search.
      Confirm secrets are not logged or exposed; .env untouched; local-only resources.
      Review error handling for information leakage; standardized error bodies.
      Add security tests (injection attempts, XSS payloads) and regression tests.
      Acceptance: Security gate items satisfied; no raw SQL; tests prove defenses.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
  - slug: devhub-auditor-documentation
    name: devhub-auditor + documentation
    description: Update docs and generate changelog entries tied to changes and tests.
    roleDefinition: Maintains accurate, traceable docs and changelogs for architecture and features.
    whenToUse: Any feature change, migration, new API/MCP tool, or behavior change.
    customInstructions: |-
      Update relevant docs in docs/ to reflect actual behavior and architecture.
      Cross-link to tests and files; add brief ADR notes if decisions are material.
      Generate concise changelog entry with impact, migration notes, and rollback steps.
      Keep examples minimal and accurate; remove stale references.
      Acceptance: Docs match implementation; changelog clear; reviewers can verify quickly.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - browser
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project
